  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper derives analytical scaling laws for entanglement in MPS representations of smooth functions and uses them to build O(N)-gate quantum circuits for amplitude encoding. The method prepares probability distributions (normal, log-normal, Lévy, Gamma) and is experimentally executed on IBM devices with up to 25 qubits (passing KS statistical tests with 5000 shots) and up to 64 qubits qualitatively using Tensor Cross Interpolation–generated circuits. Reported encoding errors are low, with single-layer circuit infidelity around 10^-3–4×10^-3 on simulators.",
